# K6 - Org-sync as a saga: failure modes. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K6-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K6 - every failure site of the org-sync saga has a compensation and a test
CATEGORY Workflow
NAMESPACE TrK6NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K6 Sandbox AS trk6
    DEFINE COMPONENT Saga Failure Sites AS sites
    DEFINE COMPONENT Saga Tests AS sagatests
    # Same saga as workflows.adl (TR-W5, TR-W6, TR-W9, TR-W10); the kata audits it, it does not redefine it.
    DEFINE SAGA Org Sync Saga AS org-sync-saga-audit
        DEFINE COORDINATION Choreography
        DEFINE CONSISTENCY Eventual

# Course pp. 44-45: a saga is only as safe as its compensation at each step. The compensation
# vocabulary is already workflows.adl's (block, keep, record), plus skip for a no-op. The audit
# reads every failure message in sync-org-memory.mjs and requires a declared compensation for each,
# so a new failure path cannot appear unclassified (the K4 inventory form).
ASSERT(Saga Failure Sites: every failure message in sync-org-memory.mjs has a declared compensation (block, keep, record or skip), and no declared row is stale) # [K6-01]

# A compensation nobody exercises is a claim, not a property. Existing TR-W5, TR-W6, TR-W9 and
# TR-W10 cover push failure, corrupt index, wipe and drain. The audit finds the failure modes that
# no test reaches (answers.md), pinned as a finding until each gets a test or an expiring exemption.
ASSERT(Saga Tests: every declared failure mode is exercised by a test that names it) # [K6-02]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): push failure keeps the job
# (TR-W5), corrupt index and wipe abort without touching the vault (TR-W6), drain retries and
# reconciliation (TR-W9, TR-W10), fail-closed privacy filter (TR-D3).
